{"id":"charter-schools","title":"Charter schools in San Francisco","question":"How many San Francisco public-school pupils are in charter schools, who authorised those schools, and how has the share moved?","finding":"The State directory lists 23 charter schools ever opened in San Francisco, 13 of them active. They enrolled 6,207 pupils in 2015-16 and 7,226 in 2025-26: 10.4% and 12.9% of all public-school pupils. 3,487 of the 2025-26 total are in the Five Keys schools, which the district authorised and which teach adults and people in custody; without them the share is 6.5% and 7.1%. The district authorised 19 of the 23; schools authorised by the State Board of Education enrolled 461 pupils in 2025-26.","how":"Schools and authorisers are from the State education department's School Directory; a school's authoriser is the body named in the directory's district field. Enrolment is each school's autumn count of pupils in kindergarten to grade 12 from the State's school-meal eligibility files, 2015-16 to 2025-26. The share divides by the pupils of all public-school units in San Francisco from the federal file (State file for 2025-26).","limits":"Charter schools are public schools that parents choose; a rising or falling share says nothing about the quality or cost of either kind. Charter schools' own finances are not in any file on disk, so what they receive and spend per pupil cannot be set beside the district's. The Five Keys schools enrol adults as well as young people, so their numbers are not all San Francisco children. A school listed as closed may have merged into another on the list.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"school","t":"Charter school","type":"org"},{"k":"authoriser","t":"Authorised by","type":"text"},{"k":"status","t":"Status","type":"text"},{"k":"grades","t":"Grades","type":"text"},{"k":"opened","t":"Opened","type":"date"},{"k":"closed","t":"Closed","type":"date"},{"k":"first","t":"Pupils, first year on file","type":"int"},{"k":"firstYear","t":"Year","type":"text"},{"k":"latest","t":"Pupils, latest year on file","type":"int"},{"k":"latestYear","t":"Year","type":"text"},{"k":"peak","t":"Most pupils","type":"int"},{"k":"peakYear","t":"Year","type":"text"},{"k":"note","t":"Note","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"school":"Five Keys Independence HS (SF Sheriff's)","schoolKey":"FIVE KEYS SCHOOLS PROGRAMS","authoriser":"School district","status":"Active","opened":"2008-09-02","closed":null,"grades":"10-12","first":1925,"firstYear":"2015-16","latest":2734,"latestYear":"2025-26","peak":3738,"peakYear":"2019-20","note":null},{"school":"Thomas Edison Charter Academy","schoolKey":null,"authoriser":"School district","status":"Active","opened":"1998-08-25","closed":null,"grades":"K-8","first":693,"firstYear":"2015-16","latest":614,"latestYear":"2025-26","peak":734,"peakYear":"2017-18","note":null},{"school":"Mission Preparatory","schoolKey":null,"authoriser":"School district","status":"Active","opened":"2011-08-15","closed":null,"grades":"K-8","first":264,"firstYear":"2016-17","latest":494,"latestYear":"2025-26","peak":494,"peakYear":"2025-26","note":null},{"school":"Gateway High","schoolKey":null,"authoriser":"School district","status":"Active","opened":"1998-08-31","closed":null,"grades":"9-12","first":482,"firstYear":"2015-16","latest":475,"latestYear":"2025-26","peak":519,"peakYear":"2020-21","note":null},{"school":"The New School of San Francisco","schoolKey":null,"authoriser":"State Board of Education","status":"Active","opened":"2015-08-17","closed":null,"grades":"K-8","first":77,"firstYear":"2015-16","latest":461,"latestYear":"2025-26","peak":461,"peakYear":"2025-26","note":null},{"school":"Creative Arts Charter","schoolKey":null,"authoriser":"School district","status":"Active","opened":"1994-09-07","closed":null,"grades":"K-8","first":414,"firstYear":"2015-16","latest":420,"latestYear":"2025-26","peak":441,"peakYear":"2022-23","note":null},{"school":"City Arts & Leadership Academy","schoolKey":null,"authoriser":"School dis